n},\\;q\\in[-\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)^2]","ascii":"Central 3 by 3 differences of the calibrated field give gradient g and Hessian H in the orthogonal pixel basis. The smallest eigenpair (lambda, n) defines q = -(g dot n) / lambda * n / spacing. A valid interior cell is a ridge when lambda < 0, -lambda >= minimumCurvature, center >= minimumValue and each q component is in [-0.5, 0.5). Half-cell ties select the larger column/row; equal eigenvalues choose the column normal. Strength is max(0, -lambda) at every valid stencil. Borders and stencils with missing or nonfinite samples write zero to all outputs. Geographic/Web Mercator ground scales are row-local tangent approximations, not a covariant Hessian or a material-LCS test.","symbols":[{"id":"normal","role":"intermediate","binding":"wgsl:normal"},{"id":"eigenvalue","role":"intermediate","binding":"wgsl:smallest"},{"id":"offset","role":"intermediate","binding":"wgsl:pixelOffset"},{"id":"gradient","role":"intermediate","binding":"wgsl:gradient"},{"id":"spacing","role":"parameter","binding":"wgsl:spacing"},{"id":"ridge","role":"output","binding":"wgsl:ridges"}]}],"sources":[{"id":"wgsl:560dede8","language":"wgsl","moduleId":"GPUScalarFieldRidges","hash":"560dede8","bodyHash":"960fbe74","entryPoint":"main","textLines":[[0,16],0,16,0,0,[17,4],0,[21,16],25,[37,6],20,0,0,[43,8],20,0,[51,5],20,56,0,[57,19],25,[76,12],25,[88,29],25,20]}]},"decisions":[],"choices":[{"stage":"operator","name":"minimumValue","value":0,"sweepable":true},{"stage":"operator","name":"minimumCurvature","value":1,"sweepable":true},{"stage":"support","name":"cellSizeMode","value":"uniform","sweepable":false}],"metrics":[{"schema":"luma.computation-metrics/1","runId":"run-42a32b13","executionId":"d1d7362b-ad23-45f4-a523-ce6729927f0b","graph":"gpu-raster-scalar-field-ridges-compiled","timebase":"ms","encoding":{"coalesced":false,"timestamped":true,"taps":1,"lensTwin":true},"nodes":{"scalar-field-ridges-ridges":{"cpuEncodeMs":0.10000002384185791,"gpuBegin":0